<title>SINGAPORE: Lum Chang first-half net surges 190 pct.</title>
<headline>Lum Chang first-half net surges 190 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Dec 31 1995</p>
<p>	     (in million of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     8.93   vs    3.08</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	 2.80   vs    1.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		     146.69   vs  102.11</p>
<p>    Other income		   4.34   vs    1.79</p>
<p>    Interest expense	     4.93   vs    3.04</p>
<p>    Operating pretax	    18.27   vs    1.42</p>
<p>    Associates		    (2.69)  vs    1.63</p>
<p>    Tax				5.27   vs   (0.82)</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (1.37)  vs    0.85</p>
<p>Note - Construction and property-based Lum Chang Holdings Ltd said the significantly higher net profit was mainly due to profit recognised from the progressive completion of its Emerald Green condominium project.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
